      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-07-11_WidnesExaminer_art0009" n="art0009">
        <head>PRICE ONE PENNY</head>
        <p>PRICE ONE PENNY</p>
        <p>Br Porr} 7id per Quart4r. 6s.6d.per Annum iced-per Quarter eredit</p>
        <p>FURNISH AT WORSLEY'S,</p>
        <p>THE MAMMOTH HOUSE FURNISHERS, "THE PANTHEON," GAYTHORN, MANCHESTER.</p>
        <p>HE EMPORIUM OF THE WORLD FOR HIGH-CLAS</p>
        <p>SECOND-HAND FURNITURE. • WEEKLY CHAT.</p>
        <p>Among the many interesting subjects which are occupying the human brain, none at this .season of the year is more im- portant than •• House Furnishing." As one of the best guides to house furnishing is obtained by personal visits and ocular demonstration, we should recommend all intending pur- chasers to pay a visit to "The Pantheon," Gaythorn, Man- chester, perhaps the very largest and most complete furnish- ing establishment in the world so largely devot,yl to the sale of high-class Second-hand Furniture. WOWSLEY'S have duly accredited agents throughout the country buying the best specimens of hand-made, high-class, genuine Second- hand Furniture, by the very best makers, such as Lamb, Gillows, Ogden, Doveston, Garnett, &amp;C. It is a fact indisputable that you can obtain at Worsley's Massive Second-hand Furniture equal, if not better, thau any new, at prices positively less than the new common London furniture. As an example of what Worsley's can offer we illustrate it best by citing a Massive Vine Old Spanish Mahogany Sideboard, 6ft. 6,n. long, in magnificent rich- coloured wood, splendidly figured—a perfect picture. This sideboard would cost original y quite 70 to 80 guineas ; Wore- ley's price, £l2. This bargain is worth a dozen of the new sideboards of to-day at £l2. We could give hundreds and thousands of such bargains, in fact Worsley's can fit you up at prices simply astounding; they have a, large cabinet fac- tory, and employ over 60 men manufacturing the bulk of their new stock.</p>
        <p>THE PANTHEON. A visit to The Pantheon will well repay the trouble. It is one of Manchester's warehouses of immense size, close to the Centtal Station ; occupies nearly a million square feet of showroom, fitted throughout in ith the electric light ; .has lifts to all the floors and contains ten times the stock of furniture of any other house in Manchester. All the showrooms are well lighttd, easy of access, you can see what you are purchas- ing, examine it thoroughly, and, best of all, you can please earselves whether you buy or n )t, No salesman is allowed toundssly press a customer to purchase.</p>
        <p>SPEd CAL BM-MAINS. Out of the Thousands of Bargains on view at the Pan- theon, Gaythorn,we sele3t a few which are enumerated below, space preventing a full and adequate description. Kindly note the following: FOR CASH OR GRADUAL PAYMENTS. WORSLEY'S ALLOW CREDIT to any respectable purchaser. LIST o—f—Co-----'mplete HOUSES ot FURNITURE. ALL WONDERFUL BARGAINS. The first Lot is an excellent HOUSE of FURNITURE, pur complete for Four Rooms, Hall, Stairs. Landing. tte., chased and removed from Great Western-street; honestly worth £4O, our price £2O. - Lot 2. --A COTTAGE HOUSE, completely and beautift 11 y FURNISHED for £l5 containing every requisite,worth £35 write for particulars. Lot 3. A most useful, substantial House of Furniture for dining-room, kitchen two bedrooms. sundries for scullerY hall, stairs, landing, for £4O • the sideboard in the din- ing room originally cast £3O. This isa rare bargain; first come first served. Will be stored free until required upon pay. ment of 5 per cent. deposit. Lot 4. A downright good HOUSE of FURNITURE for a Lancashire lad who is house proud and admires a comfortable home. In the first place there is one of the handsomest • Spanish Mahogany Sideboard Dressers, with carved back, fitted with mirrors,the prettiest ever made ; the Sofa, 'hairs. and Arm Chairs are all hair. The Bedroom contains a proper- Lancashire Bedroom Suite,strong well made,ail solid Ameri- can walnut. A massive brass-mounted Bedstead with spring mattress, hair mattress. &amp;c. There is everything required besides, such as carpets, oilcloths, fenders, fireirons,chamber service, rugs ; but space prevents us giving full particulars ; Iwe will send full particulars if you will write for them. I Price for the lot complete, £39 9s Ed. Guaranteed for 10 ' years.—WOKSLEY'S. Lot 5. The best House of Furniture in England for £5O delivered. Write for particulars. Lot 6. Excellent opportunity for matrimonial candidates. A very pretty HOUSE OF FURNITURE, only recently furnished to order by a good provincial house. Worsley's can offer an exceptional bargain. *the lot complete cost £250, anti is furnished in exquisite style, and is now no worse than new, being perfectly clean and fresn. Price for the lot, £B5 15s. When we say it contains solid FurniturcearfporDs raan7l- ing, Dining, and two B m ,KI Roos, besides all the sundries for Kitchen, bervant's Bedroom, Hall Furniture. et Linoleum for all Rooms, there is no further need to say it is a bargain. Come and see for ourself. A complete list for- warded to anyone tiking the trouble to writa for it. Lot 7. A HOUSE OF FURNITURE. plain, but strong and useful, suitable for shooting box, seaside dwelling, or small country house; price £lB 10s. Lot 8. A Semi-detached HOUSE OF FURNITURE (rent of house was £5O) The whole of this furniture, including a new Neurneyer pianoforte, is in splendid condition, contains drawing-room, dining-room, sittin4-r ,om, four bedrooms, servants' room, hall, kitchen, full cellars. No arpets or oilcloths, simply all tha heavy furniture wil' be.offered by Worslev's, in one lot or separate. In one lot for £l5O, cost nearly 140 J. Particulars supplied post free.</p>
        <p>_ GREAT BARGAINS IN DOI 'Th--7-7-1 br-ROO/4 FURNITURB. Lot 150. A Magnificent Solid Oak Dining,room Suite, by Garnett, consisting of a magnificent suite of couch, two easy chairs, and 12 single chairs, in morocco, stuffed all through with finest curled hair ; a splendid suite, beautifully uphol- stered, comfortable and luxurious ; price 20 guineas,cost £B5. The Sideboard is all solid oak to mateh, is a fine specimen of good cabinet work; price £l4, cost £45. The massive 10 feet Dining Table to match for 28, cost £25, ilhe suite complete if in one lot, for £4O; suite. sideboard, and table the cheapest, lot in Groat Britrin. Inspcci at . once, or will be eold.— ••O Lot 179. A Very Massive Solid Oak Dining-room Suit, Marsden and Banning, consisting of suite of .5 pieces, coif is, two easy chairs, and 12 high-class standard padded back single chairs, late the property of a nobleman ; the suite alone must have cost £l5O to £2OO. It is upholstered-In Morocco and has a set of loose covers ; our price for the lot only 20 euine is. The sicleb, arc' 'a magnificent, both in design and quality ; the back is divided in three parts, sur- mounted with a beautiful Corinthi in cornice and capitals, three bril.iant crystal mirrors are elegently fitt d in the re- cesses : the lower part is also massive and elegently fitted ; price only £3 i, worth £l2O. &amp; fine 12 feet dming table to match for £l5 155., cost £45. A splendid cvermantel to- match, cost £3O, for £9 10s. Anyone requiring really high- class second-hand furniture ought to inspect this lot at once only requires to be teen to effec•-, a speedy clearance. Lot 213. A Spanish Mahogany Dining-room Suite, com- plete, with 9-piece dining-room suite of conch, two easy chairs, and six fine massive single chairs in morocco, massive 7-feet Spanish mahogany sideboard, aod it 10-feet Spanish mahogany dining table on heavy carved supports the whole lot tor £2s. would cost £1.20 new won r, ,rs G REAT BARGAINS IN DRAW iNG-itowsl- - I URE. Lot 516. A DRAWING-ROOM, one of the roost perfectly furnished rooms imaginaNle, containing furniture of the most stylish. recherche. fascinating description. The whole in carved Chippendale, being dull polished so highly appreciated new in society, and although second-baud Is quite perfect, so perfect that it would puzzle an uphol- sterer to tell it had been used. .all that art could do hav- ing just been completed to make the furniture equal to new, it neing essential that drawing-room furniture should be sp tiessly fresh. The suite contains s:ttee. two Princess easy chairs, a carved back chair, and four variously designed occa- sional chairs, the whole being upholstered in rick Genoa velvet. The cabinet is sft ; Mooresque in style, having a Moorish carved curtain canopy ; the whole is britliantly fitted with curiously shaped panels of bevelled plate glass, the lower portion containing china encasements. The overmantel matches, the coal cabinetsiditto, and last, but not least, there is a set of four occasionalt shies of wierd style,eaeh different. The whole, as before stated, forms a charming suite, well worth 250 guineas • price for immediate sale 85 guineas. In- spection . H.WORSLEY, Gaythorn, Manchester. Lot 753. A Magnificent Drawing-room Suite, second hand,. but equal to new,tu •:A,lnu6,cost £5 i,for £l2 10s. The hued- some Ch'ff outer to uncli, with glass back and marble top, for £6 10s. Overmantel to match, 455.</p>
        <p>- Lot 593. A7i7-ei:37-Fret-ty Chippendale Drawing-room Suite. in rich silk covering, exquisitely upholstered, most stylish in design. for £l5 158 ; worth £35. Moorish Chippendale Cabinet to match. for £l5 15s. Overmantel, £3 4s. 100 Drawing-room Suites on view, £3 10s to £5O. GRb - RE AT T BARGAINS IN BEDROUhI. FURNITURE. _ . _</p>
        <p>Lot 913. Bedroom Furniture, hands3me, very bold. And of' original des gn, by Doveston, and consists of a very massive wardrobe, containing all modern fitments, with a pair of brilliant plate glass full dress fo:ding doors. The dressing table s pedestal, fitted with numerous drawers and sur- mounted with brilliant swing mirror attached to elegantly- fitted jewel drawers. The washstand is fitted with Carrara marbl too, also Carrara marble back, as superior to tiles, fitted also with shaving mirror. There is a fine table de nuit alt-o four chairs and towel airer. The wardrobe is 7ft. 6iti. ; The tables sft. The suite cost £175 ; price 65 guineas. Money returned if not satisfactory. The very heavy solid brass Persian bedstead of this room is a surprise, being un- doubtedly the lisndmomett In the North of England ; It is Atted with quadruple wire mattress and quite new hair mat- tress. Price for the lot, £2B 15s. The bedstead alone cost £5O, WONSLEY'S, Manchester.</p>
        <p>Lot 9)2. A high-case solid American walnut bedroom suite, richly and superbly carved in bas relief. This suite is if very superior style and workmanship. and Is unique horn the il.ct that it i• the only one of the kind in the world. It contains the usual pieces as in lot 3. but the sizes are 61t. wardrehe and 4ft. 61n. dressing table and washstand; the panels are all inlaid in solid American walnut with the finest figured burr walnut; price £35, worth £7O The brass Persian bedstead is similar to lot 3. but not so massive; price £l5 compete. WO ,SLHY'S, Manchester</p>
        <p>Terms of business: Goods packed and delivered free, Cathor by graduated PO ments• No abatement from advertised bargains. Everything absolutely guaranteed. W. H. WO Is LEY, " The Pantheon," 4aythorne, Manchester. City-road cars pass the door, which is quite dose to the Central Station, HOURS OF BUSINESS, 9 to 7 EVERY DAY.</p>
        <p>r I idUNTuY BUY EILS.—The enormous patron- - 1 age enjoyed by Worsley's from customers all over Lancashire, Yorkshire, Cheshire, The Potteries, all over the North, The Midlands. and Wales, will prove how much lathe saving effected by purchasing at Worsley's. In future car- riage will be paid on all ordersyer £2O to any part of Eng- land an i Wales. It is only fat, to say that better value could not be obtained than Wursiey's New GoL.ds. and the Second- hand Furniture simply bewil ere and demoralises competi- tion. Never mind what distance you live from Manchester, It will pay you to visit WBrsley's ; you will save quite st.i pet. cent.</p>
