        <p>kftsr the wedding of Princess Maud of Wales at "4ingtiara Palace, it is stated that there is to be grae,- "luncheon party, and that subsequently pro- sons Will be formed—two in number—for a tetilru to Marlborough House. The route at pre- lAnt contemplated will be via Constitution Hill, adilly, and St. James's-st., but it is very pos- d, e that the bride and bridegroom will travel pn:ect to king's Cross Station from Buckingham ,„,4111te en mutt for Sandringham. If the former at- netnent holds gooc. the bride and bridegroom ill travel together in a separate procession to gilillbcwough house, followed afterwards by the pr!IR and queen of Denmark and the Prince and Intess of Wales.</p>
