      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-07-11_WidnesExaminer_art0022" n="art0022">
        <head>WARRINGTON TOWN COUNCIL</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON TOWN COUNCIL</p>
        <p>The monthly meeting of the Council was held in the Council Chamber on Tuesday evening. The litayor (Couccilior Faircloug,h) presided, and there were also present :—Aldermen Sutton, Blackhurst, Francomb, Bolton, Wright, Hutchinson ; Councillors Hepherd, Baird, Ellison, Duncan, FurnePs, Wilkinson, Evans„ Bennett, Garner, Rogers, Lee, Robert, Heaton, Shaw Green, Longton, Shilicock, F. Monks, Tinnimm, Skelton, Plumpton ; Messrs. J. Lyon Whittle (town elerk), S. Wilson (deputy clerk), 5. Fairhurst ,(borough treasure*, T. Longdin (borough surveyor), and fladdook (gas engineer).</p>
        <p>tOLAVED ALIDERTgRN. At the openirtg of the meeting the aider Manic chairs were all vacant., and the MAYOR facetiously remarked that he did net see how they were to get on with their work as there were no aldermen present. Councillor SHAW-GRREV suggested that they might get out of the difficulty by mating one or two new aldermen. The business was, however, proceeded with And several aldermen put n an appearance shortly afterwards.</p>
        <p>_ Ttit V&amp;0110U4H EXTEYSIONI3ILL. The MANOR, on taking his seat, said •:—I have the pletsure and satisfaction of formally reporting to the 'Conrail that the Bill far confirming the arrington 'Extension Order was read a third time in the House of 'Lords last night— (heart. Ilear)--tb,nd the Bill now only cwaits the Royal assent. (Herr, hear.)</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-07-11_WidnesExaminer_art0023" n="art0023">
        <head>'IINDIttAIIn</head>
        <p>'IINDIttAIIn</p>
        <p>Tin minus of the folle-wing committeesof which the most important items were given in the " Examiner " last week were adopted without debate,:—Watctk,Com- rnittee, Hecith Committee, Sanitary 'Works Comnrittee, 'Cemetery, 'Committee, Town Hall. Perk and Baths'Com- ftnittee, PLarkets Committee, Tire l'Engine Committee, Water Committee.</p>
