        <p>MANCHESTER.</p>
        <p>A shockinv, discovery was made at Moston, near Man- chester. late on Wednys-?ay night. An old man named Robert Sewell and his sister, Ann, aged seventy, had not been seen for several days, and an entran^e into their house was forced. The oldnan was found dead, and the old woman helpless and almost unconscious. The death of the man and the alarminc.,, condition of the woman are, it is supposed, due to starvation.</p>
        <p>At Ledbury on Tuesday, Charles Hankins,7a labourer, who had had frequent quarrels with his wife, shot his two children, atzed six and two years, and afterwards committed suicide. He had had what proved to be the final quarrel with his wife only a few minutes before he committed the crime.</p>
