        <p>MESSRS. RICHMOND AND COMPANY. th_4boot6oo worktnen and friends formed m t 7 Works of Messrs. Richmond and Co. They War- atle*t time. the trip from ;,,,pgtc!n 6.30 a.m. and reached Blackpool in fair .9 ;11e tickets of the excursionists gave them free admi_. - ..12::1 to Raike's Hall, which, in consequence was largely tilercn3lEed. The numerous other places of entertain- v. tit in the town also received their share of visitors, 4tnio all enjoyed themselrei. Dinner was partaken of bp ' o'clock at the Victoria Hold. when Mr. MUMMA aided in the absence of Mr. Richmond through illness. lihrti• Richmond was present on behalf of her husband. Rl:,read a letter from Mr. Richmond, expressing his re- ttaZ.' at being absent, and in which he also alluded with I,''Bfaction to the progress in the extensions to the The dinner was made the occasion of a presen- Mr. Thornton (who is leaving to go in partner- 201D with an uncle) being made the recipient of a hand- watch which had been purchased for him din-ctors travellers, and office staff, of the firm. hoe Inornbers of trip arrived home by the 830 train al Blackpool.</p>
        <p>THE ODDFELLOWS. Th Members of the different local branches of Odd- s tow it . B clubbed together this year and a formed a rong 411f12° Party of their own. The idea originated at the 495 YearlY meeting of the Constitution Lodge in June, th, , when on the proposition of Mr. Frederick Taylor, hope!Creta...-,y of the lodge, it was decided that one be 1B9: lln connection with their lodge in the summer of doi, and that a fund, into which members desirous of ener,g,en, might pay their contributions, be at once Itr,4 T Re% S. Steel'• was ele3ted hon. secretary and .G. V • - tdW i ham Watson as lion. treasurer. It was Bug. fh4 that any other lodge in the district might open a c't its o.vo, and that when the time came the ex- -142,213,,1r1ight be of an amalgamated character. This lleii""c'h was adopted in the William Savage,Haven of tter,,' aun the Prince of Wales's Lodges, where funds Itat' °Pei:led. There was a good response, and at the •Tapirtetieg of the committee, consisting of Messrs. F. k•atin"` lehairman),W. Watson and V. S. Steel (Consti- '3. Ife,a,ll,odgel, VVT McQuire (William Savage Lodge), Woo4,ll'll' (Haven of Rest Lodge), R. Hamlett and R. the t;(Prince of Wales's Lodge), it was decided that Waii;.'l3 should take place on the Saturday following la .hitK, ,-, s'kturd ft ~"ay,and that the party should i v isit Llangollen. ailee ELY 8 trip was the outcome of this dea,aud a most 1;6,e/10111 one it proved. Such a promising inaugura- taeo%.l4l....euld impel the Oddfellowe to see that the "out " kvaii-Zr as annual one. Some 120 Oddfellows and friends .to th'm themselves of the opportunity of paying a visit Ipt.t.e beautiful vale of Llangollen. Special carriages 'cl4a`ve..ttached to the ordinary train which leit Bank ...ahoti,tlta,. tion at 8.15 a.m., and Llangollen was reached -qt. tra-i,s`y 30- The weather was fine. Tne trippers on 'et :ulll7 formed themselves into parties, and arranged itiag Some of the many interesting sights of the 'kt7; ..Bome went by 