        <p>ALL MEN ARE LIARS. S 3 writes a Popi-lar Author. Not so bad as that I hope, although I must admit some men are wicked liars; in fact, it's only by accident they ever speak the truth. It is not a lie when Gershon, the Universal Furnishing Contractor, 44, Oldham-street; 17, 19, and 21, Hilton-street. Manchester, st4tes that he never attempts to put before the public common new London made rubbish, more like orange boxes, for high-class second-hand ; it is not a lie when Gershon sta'es that he never attempts to trespass upon his neighbour's business. Why should he? It only causes u bad feeling. Gershon's motto is live and let live, lie sticks to the one thing he understands, namely, furnishing. If you can't furnish with a man that understands his business, you cannot do so with men th 4 don't. Gershon has for years cautioned the public against buying common new London furniture for second hand, and he still does so. However distasteful it may be to -others. Gershon still takes his stand upon the rock of " Honesty and Justice," which are the guiding principles of his business, and from which precepts time nor tide will cause him to recede. TERMS OF BUSINESS. RAILWAY FARE PAID TO COUNTRY CUSTOMERS. GOODS STORED FREE TILL REQUIRED. " REattEMßita." Any lot advertised may be had on the deferred payment system without any extra charge. Goods exchanged if not satisfactory. Mr. Gershon will purchase or take in exchange a single article or iomplete kouses of furniture. COMPARE PRICES.</p>
        <p>REVOLUTION IN THE FURNISHING TRADE. Mr. GERSHON is a great admirer of keen competi- tion, but he strongly objects to others copying his advertise- ments. It's mean; and to those that have not the brain power to write their own, Mr._!Gershon will do so for them. ------ DEVOLUTION IN THE FURNISHING TRADE. No extra charge 'or credit, and 5 per cent. allowed for prompt cash. Mr. Gershon is anxiously waiting to see what unscrupulous shopkeeper will copy this. -- / DE.</p>
        <p>REVOLUTION IN THE FURNISHING TR -- MARVELLOUS BARGAINS. OEMS tiON 'S CAUTION. - When in search of genuine second-1 and goods don't be de- ceived and have new common stuff, m re like orange boxes palmed on to I ou. When I have second-hind furniture give he names and addresses, and dun% simply say I get them from this place and th a place, You might as well look for a neßdle in a truss of hay as look for the late owner. Don't forget what the popular author wrote, "All men are bars."</p>
        <p>NO EXTRA CHARGE FOR CREDIT. FIVE PER CENT. ALLOWED FOR PR.ONIPT CASH. Out of the number of mansions, hotels, abd houses I have second-hand goods from, the following may be mentioned. CALL AND INSPECT IHE GOODS FROM— HAYESLEIGH, OLD TRAFFORD PRINCE OF WALES HOTI4.L, HARROGATE. HOLLY LOMA.% ALEXANDRA PARK. FULSHAW BANK. WILMSLOW. CARLTON-STREET, MWS MRS. GOLLOTT. WILM LOW. MRS, THOKBURN, UPPER BROOK-STREET, AND OTHERS.</p>
        <p>BARGAINS GREAT AND WONDERFUL. Smart complete House of Furniture, consisting of the whole furniture for three rooms, sitting-room, bedroom, full size bedstead, mattress bed,bilsttr, pillows, sheets, blankets, bolster case, pillow slips, and kitchen complete, all like new; price 14 guineas. No extra charge on the deferred payment system. Five per cent. for prompt cash. Call and inspect them. No harm done if you don't buy.</p>
        <p>MARVELLOUS VALUE. A Charming House of Furniture, really like new. It consists of dining-room suite in leather, extending dining- table, carpet, rug, fender, fire brasses, lace curtains, window pole complete, magnificent bedroom suite (not paintcd, solid wood), enclosed dressing-table, large bevelled glass attached' enclosed washstand, marble slab tile back and bevelled sbaving mirror, they form two complete clMt of drawers; full-size ,handsome blaOk and brass bedstead, wire spring mattress, bed. bolster, pillows, sheets, blankets. pillow slips, bolster cases, toilet set, carpet complete furniture for kitchen, floorcloth for same, ditto for lobby and stairs. Call and inspect the lot. Get a complete list, and you will say they are a marvel of cheapness for 24 guineas. No extra charge on the deferred payment system. Five per cent allowed for prompt cash.</p>
        <p>GERSHON'S UNIVERSAL FURNISHING ARCADE, 44, Oldham-street (next to the Adelphi Bank), Manchester. Charming Drawing-room lot, in perfect condition, con- sisting of handsome Suite, just been re-covered in one of the moat fashionable coverings : the charming Cabinet to match, lovely Overmantel, two Tab es, Carpets and Rug, Fender and Fire Brasses, all complete and ready for fit- ting up. A superior drawing-room well worth 25-,delivered for 24 guineas. NO EXTR CHARGE FOR CREDIT. FIVE PER CENT ALLOWED FOR PROMPT CASH.</p>
        <p>GERSHON, THE UN IV ERS AL FURNISH- ING CONTRACTOR, 44, Oldhatr-st., next to the Adelphi Bank, Manchester.</p>
        <p>FROM ONE of the ABOVE ADDRESSES. Remarkably handsome Solid Walnut Bedroom Suite, consisting of full 6ft.l wardrobe with two robing bevelled mirrors reaching from plynth to co nice fitted with drawers, cupbowds, and hanging comp rtments ; magnificent pedes- tal dressing table, fitted with eight drawers in the pedestals and large bevelled glass attached supported by carved brac- kets; large size pedestal washstand fitted with cupboards in the ed. stals ; bedside pedestal with napkin drawer, t wel rail, and three charming upho`stered chairs. The suite is guaranteed solid throughout. Well worth £53: packed, war- ranted, and delivered for 24 guineas. No extra charge for credit, five per cent. allowed tor prompt cash. Gershon, Universal Furnishing Contractor, 44, Oldbam-strcet, next to Adelphi Bank, Manchester. GERSHON ALLOWS FIVE PER CENT DISCOUNT FON PROMPF CASH.</p>
        <p>ANUMBER of Bedroom Suites, just like new, from a hotel, in solid American Walnut, Bur Walnut, Satin Walnut. Olive Wood, Bird's Nye Maple. Erulish Ash, Mahogany, Cyprus, and . ther wood=. Each suite includes a superior wardrobe. well-fitted and plate-glass door, bevelled ; dressing table with bevelled glass attached, some enclosed, some open. and some with side reflectors ; d .üble washstand with marble slab, tile back, and beveled shaving mirror ; bedside cupboard, chairs, and owel airer ; the prices are 18. 16, 14, 12,10 and 8 guineas the •uite, packed and delivered. Each suite is worth double. Five percent. for prompt cash. Eo extra for credit. Call and inspe .t them. CIHRS RO Universal Furnishing Contractor, 44, Oldham-A:ea, next to the Adelphi Bank, Manchester.</p>
        <p>GRAND BARGAIN IN DINING-ROOM SUITE. —All the wood work is guaranteed solid, spring stuffed, covered in dark grain le ither, all in perfect order; the 'covering is new; pr ce, packed and delivered, £4 18s 6d. Charming Suite, in saddle bags, all new cover- ing, extra strong solid frames ; grand b rgain for 5 guineas. Several Sideboards, in various woods at marvellously low prices, with bevelled glass backs; trom les to 263. Dining Tables, all sizes and all woods ; from 21s. Second-hand Carpets. Rugs, Fenders, and every requ.site for complete furnishing, at GERSHON'S. the UNIVERSAL FURNISH- ING CONTRACTOR. 44, OLDH VA-STREET, next to the Adelphl Bank, MANCHESTER. ALL ARE INVITED TO WALK THROUGH..</p>
        <p>RESULT OF UN HAP PY MARRIAGE, DIVORCE PROCEEDINGS, Sco perhaps fhe most favourable opportunity ever off 'red to those about furnishing in good style is the present. The furnishing in qu. stion has been removed from a very lwge house in th- vicinity of Ply- mouth Grove, and everything we' made to order only 14 months ago by one of the best houses in the city. The prices quoted are exactly one-half the cost. Not hint/ like a full des- cription can be given. Insp i ection s invited. Firstl* the hall is furnished with a grand dark mahogany Loud. Stand and pair chairs to match; Price 9 guineas. The dining-room is in solid black walnut of magniti-ent. ant uncommon design. To attempt anything like. a description would be a i waste of time ;to say the least, tis the most charming and unique, the dining-table extending with extra leaves, sup- ported by square legs, which are beautifully carved ; the over- mantel is such that can only be made by workmen of the highest standard ;itis a work of art. Next comes the truly magnificent Suite, Which. of course, are also in solid black walnut, and consists of 12 standard Chairs. (the price quoted is for six chairs, more can be had if required il. with double- padded backs, two extra large lounge ch irs, and a grand couch, of large size. sideboard alon. is worth £5O Os 9d, the whole forming a noble lot for high-class dining-room. price 68 guiaeas. I have also the carpets, paintings. and engravings from the same room. The drawing room is furnished in the latest style. and surpasses everything for elegance I have ever seen. Firstly, the Curio displsy cabinet at once. strikes you as being a marvel of beauty and workmanship. It possesses all the requirements o such an artistic articlet Next comes the handsome music cabinet with face frond and various divisions, lined with plush; two curious shapel tables, with fancy cut and carved legs; the overmante with diamond-shaped glasses. and recess.. for the display of nick-nacks; lastly, but by no means the least. the truly magnificent suite of double gondola settee, for any part of the room; two charming easy chairs, four occasional chairs. and two gossipy chairs. All are upholster-d in a rich silk tanestry. with raised flowers and sways. and finished with silk eordand gimp. It may be rsmarked that these fittings are suitable for only, a high-class draw in g-r,om . There are in all nine bedrooms, .space prevents all being described. The best room of all. I may here state, is suitable for a lady of\ title or a lord, it cost £l2O, and is offered for 60gs The suite is simply magnificent, the wood is perfe tty oli ti bright- polished walnut of the choicest quality, the wardrobe is 7ft wlde, fitted at either end with hanging compartments which are enclosed with brilliant bevellsd Vaxhan plate glass of shield shape, between the doors are drawers, and above are bay-shaped cupboards. with massive carved panel-, which at once displays great dexterity with the chisel. the whole is crowned with s cornice of tower like shape.the dressing table is 41t 61n. wide, pedestal design, and ay-shaped between the pedestals, which are fitted with drawers, the glass, which supported by carved brackets, is shield shape and extra large. Next comes the 4ft 61n bay-shaped washstand, with marble slab, tile, and glass back, about 4ft high, the pedestal towel rail, and upholstered chairs forms one of the finest suites money can buy. There are eight other bedrooms which contain suites at all prices, some as low as 4 guineas and some at 14, 18, and 25 guineas. The suite from the breakfast room is in saddle bags, price 8 guineas; dining table, 355; sideb ard, £7 15s; two recesses bookcases, 75s each. Another carneJ oak bookcase and a host of other articles are on view. Carpets, rugs, fenders orna- ments, paintings. china, and glass, all removed to 44, Old- ham-street, Manchester.</p>
        <p>No part of the world, inviting settlers, offers brighter pro „ pects to the Agriculturist than</p>
        <p>ONTARIO. Descriptive Pamphlet with Maps, sent free on applica- tion to the ONTARIO Government Agency, 7. James-street, Liverpool. a</p>
