        <p>RUNCORN PETTY SESSIONS. MONDAY.—Before Messrs. A. Thomas and J. W. Lightburn, DRUNKENNESS.—For this cfrance the fAlowing persons were de sit with: Gro-ge Furnival and Ann Shaw. A warrant was issued ag dust Christopher Hough, 35, Cartwright-street, who did not appear to answer his summons. OBSTRUCTION.—George and John Percival, farmers, Park- Bile, Aston. were fined is. and costs, ror allowing a cart to remain on the highway all night without anyone in charge, on July 27th. ASSAULT —Rowland Hughes. 15. Briscoe-street. waterman, was summoned for assaulting a boy named Joseph Prescott, on the Ist July. Defendant was fined is. and 11s. costs ICENSING.—Thomas Iti-hardson was granted pertnission to sell at the Bull's Head, Halton-road, late in the occupation of William Pownall. AN UNFORTUNATE MARRIAGE.—Edward Ivens was Sum- moned for deserting Jane Ivens, his wife. Mr. Allen appeared for complainant and stated that he applied for separation and maiatainance o‘ders against the defendant on behalf of his client. He expl in d that the parties were married in April last and about six weeks later defendant deserted ker and had not co,ttribut,ed to her maintainance. She was afraid to live with him as he abused her. Defendant had had two wives one of whom was drowned a few weeks after marriage.—Defendant alleged that his wife declined to look after his first wife's children. The Bench granted a separation order, with a maintainauce order of 7s. 63. per week with costs. SCHOOL CASES —The followinz were fined f a. not sending their children to school : Alfred Baxter, 23, Surrey-street, William Lev,..r, Lostock Gralam, and John Nicholls, kuncorn.</p>
